  Grayswandir for a Rogue requires either using at least one wish or
changing alignment and #offering.


  Frost Brand:  3 skill slots to get to Skilled, and destroys potions.
  Silver Saber: 3 skill slots to get to Skilled.
  Twoweaponing: 3 skill slots to get to Skilled.

  FB & SS & 2weap take twice as many skill slots as Expert daggers.  
If Frost Brand can be obtained at all.

  They also take twice as many blessed scrolls of Enchant Weapon.


  Rogues can be Expert with their starting daggers by XL:6.




  The AC cost for twoweaponing is a result of not being able to wear a
shield.   

    +5 small shield  = 6 AC.  
    +5 Silver Shield = 7 AC.
    +5 Elven shield  = 9 AC.
 
  Note: 9 AC is the same as +0 Dragon Scale Mail, i.e.  Not twoweaponing
lets you wear an extra suit of +0 Dragon Scale Mail, not to mention the
(XL+1)/2 average backstab bonus per hit.


  That's the cost of doing less damage.



  This is especially important in the Ascension Run:

  - You'll be mobbed (With no escape once you leave the dungeon).
    - #twoweaponing affects one monster
    - AC affects all attacks: up to 8x multiplier effect.
      - Assume 4 monsters, average damage reduction 3: 
        - 12 less damage per turn partially mobbed.
  - You shouldn't be fighting anyway.


  The lesson is:  Don't bring a knife to a gun fight.  Bringing two
knives isn't any better.



